<p>In the latest turn in the U.S.-Iran maritime standoff, President Trump said on April 23 that the U.S. Navy should &quot;shoot and kill&quot; any small boats laying mines in the Strait of Hormuz. The same day, the Pentagon said U.S. forces had boarded a second tanker in the Indian Ocean, describing it as a stateless vessel carrying Iranian oil. Meanwhile, Iran circulated video that appeared to show its forces seizing two container ships in the strait and taking them toward Bandar Abbas, with Tehran casting the move as retaliation for recent U.S. interdictions. The confrontation is testing an already fragile ceasefire and putting more strain on shipping through one of the world’s most important energy chokepoints, where about 20% of globally traded crude oil and natural gas passes in peacetime. Reports across outlets say the latest cycle of ship seizures, threats and mine concerns has pushed oil prices higher and added to uncertainty for commercial shipping and seafarers, even as several countries moved to check on the safety of roughly 40 crew members from the seized vessels.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TYAUB-afO5wk3hojzA65idE2AIKCcoYPypzmp8lnqw1COszvRwXWLXTwzMtvuworP4M1ll3iH0KzxtgKT8S1WtqaczXz2ITGbyC1ylEWQkYagy5wJe26xv-1P0dtay3SQKCaSKm16jWb_pDAcVyFTBLUe379VJHy6nrXv501BGOvtI31nfIfEMiFJ-mrgv00KgoMxJzwNLDoL4xLOH0ZcR3IWBswF5QpoL75YiLcxESnAwVUWynC3ibfUZ1umYSroRs6w0hDcU4Llq4BJg' alt='Ships and boats in the Strait of Hormuz, Musandam, Oman, April 22, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Crew safety: The two seized container ships had about 40 crew aboard, and countries including India sought information on their welfare. The Hindu reported that at least one Indian seafarer was among those detained.</li><li>Mine timeline: Some reports said Pentagon briefings to Congress estimated that fully clearing mines from the strait could take up to six months, though Pentagon officials later publicly disputed that timeline.</li><li>Shipping giant: One of the seized ships was operated by MSC, described as the world’s biggest container shipping group, and another was chartered by the company. That underscores how directly the crisis is hitting major global logistics operators.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: The Pentagon said it boarded another tanker in the Indian Ocean to disrupt illicit networks providing material support to Iran, and Washington framed the action as enforcement against sanctioned Iranian oil shipments. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/23/world/middleeast/us-iran-oil-tanker-indian-ocean-mt-majestic-x.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Iran: Tehran said the ship seizures were retaliation for U.S. captures earlier in the week and argued that there can be no peace talks while the United States maintains a blockade of Iranian ports. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-trump-orders-shoot-and-kill-on-mine-laying-boats-in-strait-of-hormuz/live-76903459'>DW</a>)</li><li>Commercial shipping states: Governments linked to the crews focused less on the military signaling and more on the immediate welfare of seafarers, seeking confirmation of their safety and access after the ships were taken toward Bandar Abbas. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/iran-takes-seized-ships-port-countries-seek-info-seafarers-safety'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/article/3351209/trump-says-navy-will-shoot-and-kill-boats-laying-mines-strait-hormuz'>Trump says Navy will ‘shoot and kill’ boats laying mines in Strait of Hormuz</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-trump-video-strait-of-hormuz-ship-attack-ceasefire-lebanon/'>Iran touts video of ship seizures as Trump keeps quiet on his next move</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/trump-orders-us-navy-to-destroy-boats-laying-mines-in-hormuz'>Trump orders US Navy to destroy boats laying mines in Hor